  "raw": {
    "https://www.duq.edu/life-at-duquesne/career-development/index.php": {
      "title": "Planning for a Successful Career",
      "description": "Planning for a Successful Career Privacy policy statement. Our privacy policy has recently been updated. Dismiss Privacy Policy Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Main Menu Academics Explore All Programs Office of the Provost Our Learning Approach Colleges & Schools Academic Advising & Support Academic Catalog Academic Calendar Study Abroad Admissions & Aid How to Apply Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Us Request Info For Admitted Students Admissions Counselors Student Accounts Life at Duquesne Our Campus Housing & Dining Health, Recreation and Wellness Career Development Student Life Student Organizations & Activities Student Services Graduate Student Life International Student Life Research Undergraduate Research Graduate Research Faculty Research Centers & Institutes Social Impact Mission & Spiritan Values Opportunity, Community Building and Engagement Volunteering Opportunities Community & Global Service About Fast Facts Leadership Policies & Initiatives Faculty & Staff Directory Departments & Offices Accreditation Consumer Information Contact Us Athletics Giving News & Stories Events Information For Parents & Families Current Students Admitted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni In this section Life At Duquesne Planning for a Successful Career More in This Section Career Preparation Our Campus Campus Safety Campus Map Commuting to Duquesne Our Pittsburgh Community Parking Housing & Dining Dining at Duquesne Student Housing Health, Recreation & Wellbeing Counseling Services Health Services Recreation Services Career Development Students Career Fairs Employers Events Alumni Center for Student Involvement Commuter Affairs Disability Services First-Year Development Greek Life Parent Relations Student Services Bookstore Computer Store Computing & Technology Services Disability Services DU CARES First-Year Development First Generation Orientation Parking Student Banking UPass Student Life Graduate Student Life International Student Life Cultural Ambassadors UPass Program DU Cares Our Traditions Prepared for Anything Ask upcoming Duquesne graduates how they feel about the next step in their lives and\n                                 you'll hear a common theme: \"Prepared.\" We'll support your development of professional\n                                 confidence, impressive experience, and powerful networks you need to get a running\n                                 start on a meaningful career. Duquesne's Center for Career Development Whether you are a student just beginning college or a Duquesne University graduate,\n                                 the Center for Career Development is here to support you at every stage of your professional\n                                 journey. We help students and alumni explore careers, connect with employers, and\n                                 develop professional and job search skills through programs, events, and one-on-one\n                                 career counseling. Throughout your professional life, we'll always be in your corner. The relationships\n                                 you make here—with your peers, faculty, and the entire Duquesne family—are supportive\n                                 inspiring and never stop giving. Career and Major Exploration with Focus 2 Career Duquesne’s Center for Career Development is here to help you find a major and career\n                                 path that is right for you!  Students and alumni can utilize Focus 2 Career, Duquesne’s\n                                 online career, major and education exploration planning system for helping you choose\n                                 a major, build your career goals and learn important job information. Focus 2 Career\n                                 gives you free access to a wide range of career assessments that help you explore\n                                 your values, skills, interests and personality. Based upon your results, it then makes\n                                 suggestions of possible career paths and Duquesne majors that could be a fit for you.\n                                 It also links you to important career information and resources to help you evaluate\n                                 your options and make an informed decision. Students, sign in using your MultiPass credentials to get started! If you are an alumni,\n                                 you can create your free account by using the access code DUKES. Focus 2 Career Students Focus 2 Career Alumni Graduate Outcomes Our Graduate Outcomes surveys are comprised of students who graduated in August 2022,\n                                    December 2022, and May 2023. VIEW THE FULL REPORTS Go to the previous card. Go to the next card. 95% career outcomes rate Individuals reported being employed, continuing education, completing volunteer service,\n                                                or serving in the military. 76% of those continuing education reported they will attend Duquesne University. 83% had one or more career-related internships For our students, the average number of internship experiences reported was 4. Upcoming Events All career prep events Let's Do Lunch: Resumes Whether you have updated your resume several times or are just starting to think about one, learn how to craft a strong document that you feel confident about! We are pleased to host Fastenal as our employer guest for this session. Sep. 09, 2026 12:00 pm - 12:45 pm Union 613 More About This Event Let's Do Lunch: Healthcare Resumes This event is tailored towards Healthcare jobs and career paths, but all are welcome.  For a more general resume session, check out \"Let's Do Lunch: Resumes\" on Wednesday, September 9 at 12:00pm. We are pleased to host St. Barnabas Health Systems as our employer guest for this session. Please RSVP in Sep. 10, 2026 12:15 pm - 01:00 pm Union 119 More About This Event JCPenney Suit-Up Duquesne students, alumni, faculty, staff, and friends are invited to shop at the Mall at Robinson location for JCPenney Suit-Up! Participants enjoy an extra 30% off (up to a total of 45%) on select merchandise, including career wear, suits, business casual, jewelry, and more with coupons available Sep. 13, 2026 03:00 pm - 06:00 pm JCPenney - Mall at Robinson More About This Event Hear from Students and Alumni Learn More Go to the previous testimonial. Go to the next testimonial. You'll be surprised at what they can offer you if you just stop by and say hello.\n                                                It doesn't matter whether you know what you want to do or not. Jeffrey Brown Jr. '23 Information Technology and Digital Development Program at WESCO I began utilizing DukesConnect to network with fellow Dukes and it's been so\n                                                much more than a social network for me, it's been a lifeline! Not only have I connected\n                                                with alumni and Career Center staff, but it's great for virtually networking during\n                                                these crazy times with events such as Coffee and Connections or Dining with Dukes.\n                                                If you're not utilizing this resource, sign up now! Heather Paytas '00 When I participated on the DU Career Center's Career Road Trip to the Columbus\n                                                Blue Jackets, it helped me to take initiative on my own career in sports. We got the\n                                                chance to talk with Duquesne Alumni who have made it to the executive level of their\n                                                organization and learn first hand what it takes to get there. Maria Doench '22 Event Services Coordinator, Texas Rangers Baseball Club Meeting with my Career Consultant throughout my time at Duquesne and even as\n                                                an alumni has benefited me in my job search by giving me the confidence that my resume\n                                                is as polished as possible. Daniel Oldak '23 Supply Planner - Berlin Packaging Meet the Team Go to the previous profile. Go to the next profile. Nicole Feldhues Executive Director, Center for Career Development Kate Sheridan Associate Director, Alumni and Employer Networks Kim Pierce Coordinator, Recruiting, Data, and Systems Julie Brand Assistant Director/Career Consultant for Business Bethany Gary Assistant Director/Career Consultant for Liberal Arts and Music Ken Lawson Assistant Director/Career Consultant for Pharmacy, Nursing, and Health Sciences Lauren Watson Assistant Director/Career Consultant for Education, Science and Engineering Lynn Schwartzmiller Office Manager Let's Connect. We are excited to connect with you, our valued students, alumni, and employers, to\n                                    determine how we can best support you. Center for Career Development Schedule an appointment with your Career Consultant via Handshake or contact us (412) 396-6644 careerdevelopmentFREEDUQUESNE 614 Gormley Student Union Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Request info Apply Visit campus LinkedIn YouTube Instagram Facebook Twitter 600 Forbes Avenue Pittsburgh, PA 15282 (412) 396-6000 admissionsFREEDUQUESNE Academics Admission & Aid Life at Duquesne Research Social Impact About Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Work at DU Community Building Title IX Duquesne Portal Contact Campus Map Information For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Community Partners & Employers Copyright © 2026 Duquesne University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Accessibility ©"
    },
    "https://www.duq.edu/research/faculty-research/index.php": {
      "title": "Office of Research & Innovation",
      "description": "Office of Research Privacy policy statement. Our privacy policy has recently been updated. Dismiss Privacy Policy Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Main Menu Academics Explore All Programs Office of the Provost Our Learning Approach Colleges & Schools Academic Advising & Support Academic Catalog Academic Calendar Study Abroad Admissions & Aid How to Apply Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Us Request Info For Admitted Students Admissions Counselors Student Accounts Life at Duquesne Our Campus Housing & Dining Health, Recreation and Wellness Career Development Student Life Student Organizations & Activities Student Services Graduate Student Life International Student Life Research Undergraduate Research Graduate Research Faculty Research Centers & Institutes Social Impact Mission & Spiritan Values Opportunity, Community Building and Engagement Volunteering Opportunities Community & Global Service About Fast Facts Leadership Policies & Initiatives Faculty & Staff Directory Departments & Offices Accreditation Consumer Information Contact Us Athletics Giving News & Stories Events Information For Parents & Families Current Students Admitted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni In this section Research Office of Research & Innovation More in This Section Faculty Research Centers and Institutes Empowering Students Through Hands-On Learning Center for Migration, Displacement and Community Studies (CMDCS) Carl G. Grefenstette Center for Ethics in Science, Technology, and Law Institute for Ethics and Integrity in Journalism Center for African Studies Center for Catholic Faith and Culture Chronic Pain Research Consortium Simon Silverman Phenomenology Center Small Business Development Center Faculty Research Research Development Innovation - Creation - Technology Transfer Research Conduct Faculty Support Funding Nanomedicine Manufacturing Lab Graduate Research Graduate Research Symposium Undergraduate Research Undergraduate Research & Scholarship Symposium Supporting Research and Innovation The Office of Research and Innovation (ORI) supports and encourages faculty and students\n                                    to engage in research and innovation. As a one-stop source of information, the ORI\n                                    works toward the creation of new knowledge and its application through technology\n                                    transfer. The ORI encourages Duquesne researchers and innovators by: Providing technical support and networking opportunities Assisting with grant applications and competitions Fostering interdisciplinary and community partnerships Supporting creativity and innovative thinking in all academic fields All your research and innovation resources in one place Supporting scientific endeavors, academic creativity, licensing opportunities, and\n                              commercialization for economic development and job creation Supporting Research Well established and well recognized, Duquesne research is supported by the federal\n                                       and state governments, foundations, and corporate partners Proposal development Research conduct Innovation and Creation in Action Whatever your creativity or research ambitions, we have the breadth and depth to make\n                                       the most of them. We want you to become the kind of problem-solver who always thinks\n                                       bigger—and whose ingenuity is driven by compassion and empathy. We feel fortunate\n                                       to be entrusted with your goals and we want to encourage and nurture Duquesne faculty,\n                                       staff and students' innovative thinking and entrepreneurship spirit. We are dedicated\n                                       to help anyone seeking to make a difference in society by pursuing their innovations\n                                       and creations. IP and tech transfer resources Contact Us Please contact the ORI to find support with your research and innovation. Office of Research and Innovation oriFREEDUQUESNE Request info Apply Visit campus LinkedIn YouTube Instagram Facebook Twitter 600 Forbes Avenue Pittsburgh, PA 15282 (412) 396-6000 admissionsFREEDUQUESNE Academics Admission & Aid Life at Duquesne Research Social Impact About Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Work at DU Community Building Title IX Duquesne Portal Contact Campus Map Information For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Community Partners & Employers Copyright © 2026 Duquesne University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Accessibility ©"
    },
