    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187924": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Visiting Assistant Professor – Mathematics & Computer Science Duquesne University: School of Science and Engineering Location Duquesne University Open Date Jun 09, 2026 Description Position Number: 350130 The Department of Mathematics and Computer Science in the School of Science and Engineering at Duquesne University invites applications for a non-tenure-track Visiting Assistant Professor position in computer science for the 2026/27 academic year, with preference given to candidates who can also teach undergraduate courses in related disciplines. The department offers undergraduate majors in computer science, data science, mathematics, and applied mathematics, as well as a Master's degree in computer science. The successful candidate will join twenty other full-time departmental faculty.  The standard teaching load for NTT faculty is 12 credits per semester. Qualifications Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: M.S. degree and extensive applicable experience in computer science or a closely related discipline. A successful candidate who does not possess a Ph.D. will be hired as a Visiting Instructor of Computer Science. Teaching philosophy commensurate with Duquesne University's mission and values. Preferred Qualifications: A Ph.D./A.B.D. in computer science or a closely related discipline is preferred. Preference will be given to applicants who can teach a broad range of courses offered by the Mathematics and Computer Science Department, including mathematics and/or statistics. Preference will be given to the candidate with successful teaching experience at the university or college level. Alternately, the applicants may possess any equivalent combination of experience and training, which provides the knowledge, skills, and abilities required to perform the essential job functions. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with the University Community. Ability and willingness to contribute actively to the Mission of the University and to respect the Spiritan Catholic identity of Duquesne University.  The Mission is implemented through a commitment to academic excellence, a spirit of service, moral and spiritual values, sensitivity to world concerns, and an ecumenical campus community. Application Instructions Applicants are asked to submit a cover letter, resume/CV, and contact information for a minimum of three professional references. Duquesne University was founded in 1878 by its sponsoring religious community, the Congregation of the Holy Spirit. Duquesne University is Catholic in mission and ecumenical in spirit. Motivated by its Catholic identity, Duquesne values equality of opportunity both as an educational institution and as an employer. Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Duquesne University was founded in 1878 by its sponsoring religious community, the Congregation of the Holy Spirit. Duquesne University is Catholic in mission and ecumenical in spirit. Motivated by its Catholic identity, Duquesne values equality of opportunity both as an educational institution and as an employer. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings l